```{r}
#| include: false
if(!require("tidyverse")) install.packages("tidyverse")
library(tidyverse)
```

## Annual Sales Trend

```{r}
#| echo: false
#| message: false
txhousing |> 
  filter(city=="Houston") |> 
  group_by(year) |> 
  summarize(sales=sum(sales)) |> 
  ggplot(aes(x=year, y=sales)) + 
    geom_line() + 
    ggtitle("Annual Houses Sold in Houston, TX")
```

Houston's housing sales have generally trended upward over time, 
with a notable dip during the 2008 financial crisis followed by 
a steady recovery.

## Seasonal Pricing Patterns

```{r}
#| echo: false
#| message: false
txhousing |> 
   filter(city=="Houston") |> 
    group_by(month) |> 
    summarize(avg_price=sum(volume) / sum(sales)) |> 
    mutate(month=factor(month.abb[month], 
                 levels=month.abb, ordered=TRUE)) |>
    ggplot(aes(x=month, y=avg_price)) + 
    geom_bar(stat="identity") + 
    ggtitle("Average Price of Houses Sold in Houston by Month") + 
    xlab("Month") + 
    ylab("Average Sale Price") + 
    scale_y_continuous(labels = scales::dollar)
```

Average home prices show some seasonal variation, with certain 
months consistently commanding higher average sale prices than others.

## Houston vs. Other Texas Cities (2015)

```{r}
#| echo: false
#| message: false
txhousing |> filter(year==2015) |> 
    group_by(city) |> 
    summarize(avg_price=sum(volume) / sum(sales),
              num_sales=sum(sales)) |> 
    slice_max(num_sales, n=10) |>
    ggplot(aes(x=city, y=avg_price, fill = city == "Houston")) + 
    geom_bar(stat="identity") + 
    ggtitle("Average Price of Houses Sold in 2015 by City in Texas") + 
    xlab("City") + 
    ylab("Average Sale Price") + 
    scale_y_continuous(labels = scales::dollar) +
    scale_fill_manual(values = c("FALSE"="grey60", "TRUE"="firebrick"), guide="none") +
    theme(axis.text.x = element_text(angle = 45, hjust = 1))
```

Among the ten highest-volume Texas markets in 2015, Houston's average 
sale price falls in the middle range compared to cities like Austin and Collin County.

## Conclusion

- Houston's housing sales have grown substantially over the years, with a clear dip around 2008
- Home prices exhibit modest seasonal fluctuation throughout the year
- Relative to other major Texas metros, Houston remains a high-volume but moderately priced market  